7. Conclusion

Version 0.3.0 of the HMVA transforms the vibrational atlas into a disciplined, stratified model space. By replacing an unsubstantiated fibre‑bundle claim with a labelled partition of the base manifold and restricting structural comparisons to within strata, we eliminate the central mathematical over‑reach while retaining the vision of a common quantitative language for musical diversity. Neural entrainment is modelled with realistic oscillator networks, measurement bias is treated as a residual, and information‑theoretic quantities are kept firmly internal. All claims remain theoretical; the next phase must populate the atlas with data and subject its constructs to empirical test. This version is intended as a stable foundation for interdisciplinary collaboration.

