Appendix G. Additional Remarks on Future Model Spaces

G.1. Type‑C Spectral Shape Manifolds

For traditions with continuous pitch and timbral focus, the internal model space is a manifold of spectral envelopes. A spectral envelope is a positive function on frequency, and the natural metric is the Fisher‑Rao metric on the infinite‑dimensional manifold of probability densities (here, normalised power spectra). Modding out time‑warping reparameterisations yields a quotient space that is a nonlinear analogue of the orbifold construction. A rigorous treatment using Sobolev manifolds and diffeomorphic template matching (e.g., Srivastava & Klassen 2016) will be developed in a separate technical report.

G.2. Type‑R Rhythmic Automaton Spaces

Rhythmic traditions without pitch can be modelled as finite‑state automata generating timelines. The set of all such automata up to bisimulation forms a space with a metric based on the Kantorovich distance between their generated languages (using the Levenshtein distance on strings). This falls under the purview of quantitative language theory and will be elaborated when empirical rhythmic corpora are acquired.


